WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.979
Video can reveal people, routines, homes, workspaces, vehicles, and operations.

00:00:03.979 --> 00:00:08.634
A responsible program begins with purpose limitation: define the legitimate safety, security,

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:14.066
or operational need and collect only the coverage and detail required for that purpose.

00:00:14.066 --> 00:00:15.229
Respect privacy expectations.

00:00:15.229 --> 00:00:17.945
Avoid private or unrelated areas, unnecessary audio,

00:00:17.945 --> 00:00:21.824
and wider fields of view than the use case needs.

00:00:21.824 --> 00:00:24.152
Use masking or zones when possible.

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:26.867
Provide consent, notice, or signage where applicable,

00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:30.747
and obtain appropriate legal and policy review for the location.

00:00:30.747 --> 00:00:33.850
Set retention by need rather than storage capacity.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:38.117
Keep routine footage and AI metadata only as long as justified,

00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:41.609
with longer retention for documented events when policy permits.

00:00:41.609 --> 00:00:45.876
Deletion should include copies, exports, and backups under a defined lifecycle.

00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:50.143
Restrict live view, search, export, configuration, and administrative access by role.

00:00:50.143 --> 00:00:54.022
Use audit logs to record access, changes, sharing, and deletion.

00:00:54.022 --> 00:00:58.678
Protect review outcomes because labels and notes may be sensitive even when

00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:00.617
the original clip is gone.

00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:04.884
Do not use the system for harassment, covert stalking, inappropriate surveillance,

00:01:04.884 --> 00:01:09.152
or attempts to identify private individuals without lawful and legitimate authority.

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:14.583
Model descriptions should not be treated as facts about character, intent, or protected traits.

00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:18.850
Publish clear policy, train reviewers, provide a way to report misuse,

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.953
and review new use cases before enabling them.

00:01:21.953 --> 00:01:24.669
Local processing can reduce external data exposure,

00:01:24.669 --> 00:01:28.936
but responsible use still depends on transparency, access control, limited purpose,

00:01:28.936 --> 00:01:30.100
and human accountability.
